				)
			)
		)
		(property "ReqNotes" "Two supply options; the Orb Weaver blocks and boards use the first. (1) Always-on 3.3-V rail with ~OE pulled up to VCC so the bus is isolated at power-on and firmware isolates before dropping the switched rail; chosen because Ioff is specified for the data terminals only (VCC=0; 1 uA max) and the enable input is uncharacterised at VCC=0. (2) Switched target-domain rail so Ioff isolates at VCC=0 without spending a GPIO; rejected for the blocks because it hands sequencing to a rail ramp and leaves the MCU driving an enable input on an unpowered part. Either way pull ~OE up to VCC and solder exposed pad 21 per TI RGY0020A guidance without assuming an electrical tie. See design block rp2040_with_gpio_isolation_sn74cb3q3245 and docs/rp2040-gpio-isolation-design-block-plan.md."
			(at 99.06 332.74 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name yes)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
