	(text "Switched GPIO29: ${7a6a6ceb-6c8d-470b-b733-f24d95709c3b:REFERENCE} A6 (pin 7); bare pass gate, 3.3 V domain only." (at 1018.76 745.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "591c80ab-08de-5517-b87e-41a953ac8232"))
	(text "Instrument tap of ~{BUS_SW_EN} through ${76f4fd23-3b91-409c-babf-f38add95b44c:REFERENCE} (1 k); observe only." (at 1018.76 756.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a77e3c65-d07f-5dce-b475-59d606c15c1c"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 15.24 391.844592) (xy 308.7 391.844592)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "6cee1272-2935-547a-927a-fc44df2bd98e"))
	(text "OPERATION" (at 15.24 394.384592 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5a0c1559-3c5d-5d77-9a72-e858d876eaa6"))
	(text "64 ports: GPIO0-8 and GPIO10-29 are the raw pads, ISO0-8 and ISO10-29 the same pads behind one switch channel each; ~{BUS_SW_EN} and its tap ~{BUS_SW_EN}_INST leave for observation only. GPIO9 (pin 12) is the enable and has no GPIO or ISO port. Per index, GPIOn and ISOn are" (at 15.24 399.434592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3c6b037b-cac8-5991-a569-c98cd9224f92"))
	(text "one node when enabled: wire one or the other, by the far end's power domain." (at 15.24 401.974592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7af52888-1487-56b4-824e-4b2d2ebe239a"))
	(text "The ISO side is a bare pass gate: no level shift, buffer or protection. Switch I/O is rated to 5.5 V but the MCU pad behind it is limited to IOVDD + 0.3 V; pulls on the switched side reference the switched rail, never +3.3V. Unused ports get no-connect flags on the placing sheet." (at 15.24 405.784592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bc03b690-c10f-54bb-a120-55fa60887b69"))
	(text "Enable: GPIO9 drives ~{BUS_SW_EN} (active low) to the four ~{OE} pins; ${05532f4c-82f6-448d-af7d-5d0ce3bd597c:REFERENCE} (7.87 k) keeps the bus isolated from power-on; ${76f4fd23-3b91-409c-babf-f38add95b44c:REFERENCE} (1 k) makes the instrument tap. t_en 14 ns, t_dis 13 ns max at 3.3 V. Firmware: isolate, drop the rail; raise, confirm, connect." (at 15.24 410.494592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4069d58d-2dd3-556f-a8d6-6a8be96b45a7"))
	(text "Supply: always-on +3.3V for IOVDD, USB_VDD, ADC_AVDD, VREG_IN, the flash and the switches' VCC (2.3-3.6 V); the regulator makes +1.1V for DVDD. Each switch draws 1 mA typ, 2 mA max on or off (about 4 mA typ, 8 mA max total). Isolation rests on the enable, not on Ioff." (at 15.24 414.304592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "685785a5-63d0-5486-83c5-a3c9259cc2f6"))
	(text "Core: ${3f6431a7-d235-4c5b-a8c3-f3e79a8a5216:REFERENCE} 12 MHz with ${98f52652-2300-4a88-873a-5d62116cb394:REFERENCE}/${b8b46286-3ae0-4dd7-8d7c-301ef05bff89:REFERENCE} (15 pF) and ${da9e6438-2e15-4e59-87cc-3f2eecccbdf7:REFERENCE} (1 k); W25Q128 on QSPI; BOOTSEL grounds ~{USB_BOOT} (${50d3b797-b1d6-4150-862b-c3ff2698db6c:REFERENCE} 1 k to QSPI_SS, ${f62dac92-70b6-4e44-9437-327a35a1caeb:REFERENCE} 10 k up); RUN grounds pin 26 (${61e77b6c-4319-46a8-a58b-8225ead31e34:REFERENCE}, internal pull-up only), does not reset the flash, releases GPIO to high-Z. SWD is" (at 15.24 419.014592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f209efe6-010d-563c-b94c-81ec9fd1d5f8"))
	(text "not exposed. Two instances need separate sheets." (at 15.24 421.554592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d513350c-950e-5d20-9e5c-ad370ce139c7"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 15.24 432.984592) (xy 308.7 432.984592)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "f66a009b-8ce5-502b-8b6d-11ff289bd67f"))
	(text "DESIGN CONTRACT" (at 15.24 435.524592 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8bcf1513-1e90-5b07-835a-4b069f2f837d"))
	(text "RP2040 controller core and its GPIO isolation in one block: the full rp2040 core (W25Q128JVPIQ QSPI flash, 12 MHz ABM8 crystal, decoupling, BOOTSEL and RUN switches) plus four SN74CB3Q3245RGYR 8-channel bidirectional FET bus switches, with all 29 MCU-to-switch connections" (at 15.24 439.674592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6a56593a-f6de-5feb-9da3-fee4300c0cc9"))
	(text "made inside the block so that routing is placed once instead of re-drawn per board. Derived from rp2040, which remains canonical for an MCU with no isolation and is the upstream for the core half: fix core circuitry there first, then refresh here. The switch half has no upstream; fix" (at 15.24 442.214592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c0eff93e-d69c-5eb4-b4c1-2726c8577da4"))
	(text "it here. This block replaces the retired isolation-only companion rp2040_gpio_isolation_sn74cb3q3245 outright and is the only isolated form. Core parts are positionally identical to rp2040. DO NOT place this block alongside rp2040: it already contains that core. Designators are the" (at 15.24 444.754592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d649ba6a-752d-5371-b508-df3566bbe353"))
	(text "40xxx band." (at 15.24 447.294592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "58b16afd-9438-50e1-a07f-b780c6b07a05"))
	(text "Decoupling: ${1cb87ed5-69f6-4075-b8d2-782238f5e635:REFERENCE} (1 uF) is the +3.3V bulk at VREG_IN and seven 100 nF serve the nine +3.3V supply pins: ${c47c854b-1bb8-4264-9ef6-7c07d0e5b560:REFERENCE} at IOVDD 1, ${efda8890-a405-4ce6-9ad3-b04f634a15a3:REFERENCE} at IOVDD 10, ${059d64bd-c321-4fcb-b0a8-cb65d8d599e7:REFERENCE} at IOVDD 22, ${afc75855-e05f-4148-a389-4918ed910b98:REFERENCE} at IOVDD 33, and ${b993fd92-0e09-44ad-ad7e-5f8bc893a235:REFERENCE}, ${7ba5624c-94da-413f-84d4-c1489eecaedd:REFERENCE} and ${c61f46df-4504-4f23-8736-4f35298818a9:REFERENCE} at the corner of IOVDD 42, ADC_AVDD 43," (at 15.24 449.834592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "33b42496-fac6-57c7-af44-d975d83e456f"))
	(text "VREG_IN 44, USB_VDD 48 and IOVDD 49, where the routed PCB fixes the pairing. ${2ec4cb5b-c7ac-4da1-8b27-74bcde073cad:REFERENCE} bypasses the flash VCC (${8cc8a515-f16f-4003-a384-a7ebe0a902c5:REFERENCE} pin 8); ${d268313b-69de-4af2-8459-0942d3e13c69:REFERENCE} to ${a446e38b-6531-4660-bc9b-9886605c09d2:REFERENCE} bypass VCC pin 20 of ${f1eb94f6-66c1-4e98-b28a-e82013eea65c:REFERENCE} to ${7a6a6ceb-6c8d-470b-b733-f24d95709c3b:REFERENCE} in turn. The regulator's +1.1V has ${bcedcf39-e20b-4bf1-8165-b45139a8ad22:REFERENCE} at DVDD 23, ${805e76c9-a5fa-45c8-8dec-3d044d3d766d:REFERENCE} at VREG_VOUT 45 and" (at 15.24 452.374592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "990e21f3-e9fa-5722-9554-d5cc35e8aa81"))
	(text "${91298403-19a6-4a9a-9476-901e047393e5:REFERENCE} (1 uF) beside DVDD 50." (at 15.24 454.914592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cb91e5c6-add0-5f8d-9143-29dc0894d459"))
	(text "1. THE INTERFACE IS 64 PORTS AND GPIO9 IS NOT ONE OF THEM: 29 raw MCU ports GPIO0-GPIO8 and GPIO10-GPIO29, 29 switched ports ISO0-ISO8 and ISO10-ISO29, USB_D+, USB_D-, +3.3V, GND, and the enable ~{BUS_SW_EN} with its instrument tap ~{BUS_SW_EN}_INST, both for" (at 15.24 458.354592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cbce0c2c-19f9-5f44-bede-763fa00f66e4"))
	(text "observation only. GPIO9 is spent on the bus-switch enable and has no GPIO or ISO port; there is no ISO9 and no separate ~{OE} port. Any board placing this block gives up GPIO9 and inherits ~{BUS_SW_EN} as a firmware constant. tmc51x0-driver-dev-pcb puts the same signal on GPIO19" (at 15.24 461.794592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "01969b00-3c4a-5cfe-b38c-d4fa16fe039e"))
	(text "and does NOT use this block; do not align them." (at 15.24 464.334592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "726019fd-e834-5c42-a1de-afcee4bb4aa2"))
	(text "2. GPIOn AND ISOn ARE THE SAME NODE WHENEVER THE BUS IS ENABLED. Per index they are an either/or, not a fan-out. Wiring both shorts whatever sits on the always-on side to whatever sits on the switched side the instant firmware pulls ~{BUS_SW_EN} low, and neither ERC nor DRC" (at 15.24 467.774592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "56de69f8-9d44-5e6a-9be3-734c0d05cc04"))
	(text "can see it. The board chooses per signal, and the rule is the powered domain of the far end: a GPIO goes through the switch if and only if its far end sits on a switched rail. See mouse-joystick-pcb docs/interface-map.md, The Rule - Follow The Far End's Power Domain." (at 15.24 470.314592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2580284d-0452-5ccf-920d-b8a465abc8c3"))
	(text "3. THE ISO SIDE IS A BARE PASS GATE: no level shift, no buffer, no protection, no direction. Switch I/O is rated 0-5.5 V but the other end of every channel is an RP2040 pad limited to IOVDD+0.3 V, so a 5 V pull-up or a 5 V driver on an ISO pin damages the MCU, not the switch. Do" (at 15.24 472.854592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "21f79a97-63f2-5444-9fb3-84569f0160a3"))
	(text "not give ISO ports a direction shape: the gate is symmetric and they are passive by construction. Pull-ups and pull-downs on the switched side must reference the SWITCHED rail, never +3.3V, or they back-power the dead domain through the far chip's input clamps inside a block" (at 15.24 475.394592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6a2755ca-e39b-55f0-a2b9-4a95c22c6aaf"))
	(text "where the bus switch cannot see it." (at 15.24 477.934592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2fe28cff-6321-5ce6-9459-36a2aaf4a09b"))
	(text "4. THE ENABLE IS THE MCU'S, ACTIVE LOW, AND DISABLED BY DEFAULT: GPIO9 drives ~{BUS_SW_EN} to all four pin 19 inputs, with ${05532f4c-82f6-448d-af7d-5d0ce3bd597c:REFERENCE} 7.87 k to +3.3V so the bus is isolated at power-on until firmware asserts it. The enable cannot sit behind the switch it enables, and an MCU must be" (at 15.24 481.374592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5448facb-84d7-5ccb-97dc-a3943d89d9f9"))
	(text "able to connect a bus that is currently disconnected, so the board never sources it: ~{BUS_SW_EN} leaves the block only to be observed, and ~{BUS_SW_EN}_INST through ${76f4fd23-3b91-409c-babf-f38add95b44c:REFERENCE} (1 k) is its instrument tap. NEVER drive it from the board; a second driver fights the MCU and the pull-up is" (at 15.24 484.814592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c2bd3df0-68d1-58b8-9737-97c2ef306f95"))
	(text "the only thing defining the reset state. Sequencing is board policy and firmware must follow it: isolate first, then drop the rail; raise the rail, confirm it, then connect last. t_en is 14 ns max and t_dis 13 ns max at 3.3 V, so the disconnect is deterministic and instantaneous relative to" (at 15.24 487.354592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "182ee3ba-4627-5142-8949-9486dc53dc02"))
	(text "any rail." (at 15.24 489.894592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eaf76269-35ad-59f4-8e9d-7162dd520abe"))
	(text "5. SUPPLY IS THE ALWAYS-ON 3.3 V RAIL, DELIBERATELY, AND THERE IS NO Ioff SECOND LINE OF DEFENCE. One +3.3V port feeds the MCU, all four V_CC pins and the pull-up. Powering the switches from the switched domain would give free isolation through Ioff at V_CC=0 and cost no" (at 15.24 492.434592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "075adf12-5859-5fa1-8eef-292eedbb63ea"))
	(text "GPIO, and is REJECTED: it hands sequencing to a rail ramp, removes the ability to isolate before powering down, and leaves the always-on MCU driving an enable input on an unpowered part; Ioff is specified for the data terminals (V_CC=0, 0 to 5.5 V, 1 uA max) with no control-input" (at 15.24 494.974592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a8f3ec00-c92e-5870-8db4-18057f368bdb"))
	(text "condition stated, and V_IH is characterized only over V_CC 2.3-3.6 V. Isolation therefore rests entirely on the MCU holding ~{BUS_SW_EN} high, which ${05532f4c-82f6-448d-af7d-5d0ce3bd597c:REFERENCE} makes the reset default. This contradicts the catalog note on OW-MISC-SN74CB3Q3245RGYR, which recommends" (at 15.24 498.414592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5680a3d5-9dd7-5e5c-a413-5c3b4687bef6"))
	(text "switched-domain power; the block and the boards win, see kicad-libs docs/rp2040-gpio-isolation-design-block-plan.md." (at 15.24 500.954592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cb02b277-6792-5038-940e-bd05ce3203d0"))
	(text "6. IT COSTS 4 mA JUST BY EXISTING: I_CC is 1 mA typ and 2 mA max per package with the switch ON OR OFF, because the charge pump runs regardless, so four packages draw about 4 mA typ and 8 mA max continuously from the always-on rail even with every channel isolated. That" (at 15.24 503.494592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "46d72ac9-6a6d-5002-8b85-9e67b00db857"))
	(text "is the price of 1:1 coverage and it is accepted." (at 15.24 506.034592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "17f7ddd0-bebc-5bc3-acf8-992e14f31f5e"))
	(text "7. ONE CHANNEL PER GPIO, AND THREE SPARES. Pairing on the RGY-20 package is A_n = pin (n+1) and B_n = pin (19-n); A IS THE SWITCHED SIDE AND B IS THE MCU SIDE. ${f1eb94f6-66c1-4e98-b28a-e82013eea65c:REFERENCE} carries GPIO0-GPIO7 to ISO0-ISO7, ${9e60b624-265a-48c0-8d52-35e8fd746e9b:REFERENCE} GPIO8 and GPIO10-GPIO15 to ISO8 and ISO10-ISO15," (at 15.24 508.574592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "24d2e68e-ffbc-5e59-9c77-3e4b8e96bab0"))
	(text "${3f4bbeb0-c5b3-474e-b989-c818a1dc0234:REFERENCE} GPIO16-GPIO23 to ISO16-ISO23, ${7a6a6ceb-6c8d-470b-b733-f24d95709c3b:REFERENCE} GPIO24-GPIO29 to ISO24-ISO29. The three unused channels are ${9e60b624-265a-48c0-8d52-35e8fd746e9b:REFERENCE} channel 2, freed by the enable, and ${7a6a6ceb-6c8d-470b-b733-f24d95709c3b:REFERENCE} channels 7 and 8. Treatment for every spare is the same and is not arbitrary: MCU-side B pin to GND, A pin" (at 15.24 511.114592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "37445de4-ab45-5ab1-8cb2-4bdde0c4c8b4"))
	(text "left open, so no node floats on the always-on rail and no switched-side pin is a hidden hard ground." (at 15.24 513.654592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "54682eb5-d91a-5e89-a7c8-0d7f52271033"))
	(text "8. THE BOARD OWES NO-CONNECTS AND ITS OWN BIAS. Most ISO and raw ports are unused on any given board; flag them no-connect rather than leaving them dangling. Unused channels need nothing else: the pass gate has no internal buffer, so an open data pin is not a floating" (at 15.24 516.194592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "931d579f-d02b-5de7-a531-dded0847a636"))
	(text "CMOS input. Bus terminations, input bias and instrument taps are board-level or belong to the far-end block, never here. USB_D+ and USB_D- leave OUTSIDE the 27 ohm series resistors ${f4d604cc-a41b-4c5f-91fb-70f0f315fe11:REFERENCE} and ${cedf1931-96b1-4540-9d90-bcdade76c268:REFERENCE}; do not add more series resistance at the board." (at 15.24 518.734592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e2fcfe44-343c-541f-8d85-b4a694b1af18"))
	(text "9. CORE GOTCHAS CARRIED FROM rp2040 (full text in that block's description): SWD IS NOT EXPOSED, pins 24 and 25 are deliberately open and no debug-connector footprint exists in the libraries, so this block offers no debug header. Place ${c7236ed0-5587-4ce2-952d-028042e5d870:REFERENCE} (RUN) physically adjacent to" (at 15.24 521.274592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6736b535-c261-5a20-90ca-489724a9bbae"))
	(text "${338d1de6-d5e6-46a5-88e0-98b25a257c7c:REFERENCE} (BOOTSEL) on the same board edge or the one-handed hold-BOOTSEL-tap-RUN recovery gesture becomes a two-handed operation on an installed rig. ${61e77b6c-4319-46a8-a58b-8225ead31e34:REFERENCE} is the exception to that adjacency: it decouples RUN and belongs hard against pin 26 with a short return. RUN" (at 15.24 523.814592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "176efc8a-df17-5d83-a594-3778e5a219fd"))
	(text "has no external pull-up and needs none (the internal 50-80 k is the only one) and needs neither the 1 k series nor the 10 k pull-up that belong to BOOTSEL's QSPI_SS. A RUN reset does NOT reset ${8cc8a515-f16f-4003-a384-a7ebe0a902c5:REFERENCE}, so a warm reset that hangs where a power cycle works is the flash. RUN" (at 15.24 526.354592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eed52134-ca2c-5ac8-af9a-378318362a40"))
	(text "also releases every GPIO to high-Z, so the placing board must ensure each domain it controls defaults to safe on MCU reset." (at 15.24 528.894592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b4c5e46b-1124-5c6d-af53-a0a23a758088"))
	(text "10. TWO INSTANCES NEED SEPARATE SHEETS or the internal nets (RUN, ~{USB_BOOT}, QSPI_SS, XIN, XOUT, XOUTB, +1.1V, D+ and D-) silently merge between copies." (at 15.24 532.334592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1b38b5f8-899d-596f-be6b-4e0f9ead5957"))
	(group "Review page 01: 1. Controller core (1 of 2)" (uuid "f06a0572-8ade-572b-bf42-b6f0d25cb745") (members "1cb87ed5-69f6-4075-b8d2-782238f5e635" "94522ade-334e-53c2-bed1-6d4da0c79df3" "2eec0c26-4168-5db4-8b65-88e6e1789f76" "4e5f3c90-255e-5918-9bc8-c83acd2aa403" "bb50a601-5b66-51d5-bbd6-22bcf0a98206" "91298403-19a6-4a9a-9476-901e047393e5" "cc750314-5a6c-507c-969f-bbd0c0439594" "217b366d-7728-5303-8b4c-410738c2eee8" "4accba38-ef56-526a-bbf8-76e179586e06" "a44c23ec-91d5-5cb8-ba1c-93d1d3acfaa1" "c47c854b-1bb8-4264-9ef6-7c07d0e5b560" "e8deff0b-ddef-5ff4-a9d9-c2a9b5f03fb3" "88f80f41-bd81-5882-a1fb-d9e57004f955" "15be771b-558c-54cc-8049-44a331fbcc3e" "101919b2-1558-5143-b69b-fce411e8bc29" "efda8890-a405-4ce6-9ad3-b04f634a15a3" "b02ffce1-c954-5c27-8061-2023cbfdc6ff" "782b893b-9ee1-591d-8f5c-c631d814d4ad" "15d113be-b78e-5cee-9513-899ad1cf5925" "6270d881-830e-592b-8509-066b381329ed" "059d64bd-c321-4fcb-b0a8-cb65d8d599e7" "e180cfd9-8ee4-5dfe-83e2-f2fac9a728b7" "a5637693-ca60-5864-9c4d-f675d0a73b55" "c853a60c-ecbe-513a-82ac-68faa47b4fe8" "db05d9f5-cf96-563b-bb43-0634f3ce1e05" "afc75855-e05f-4148-a389-4918ed910b98" "e7d4983a-e547-51b5-a95a-6b1ebbf6c66f" "84bf5500-980d-5a80-9c14-b7508d071564" "7e768d20-f32b-5f13-879d-8ddb0da2e437" "62d9fc83-a653-589d-9533-4caf0b89e670" "b993fd92-0e09-44ad-ad7e-5f8bc893a235" "0a48ccfe-d6b8-589e-9a94-1e0e6a9bd8f3" "6e821b57-7e61-58d1-9e80-0d8b1894a975" "f5b0f948-56a1-53df-acef-b07bed7306df" "bb25aea6-733a-591a-9fd4-4a7a7c8959b2" "7ba5624c-94da-413f-84d4-c1489eecaedd" "38adb9dc-c03c-5d53-bbb8-db1a2a96e925" "8c1aff4f-3b2a-53ae-ad06-2673252fc1a5" "8d187089-2dd7-5eb4-a97c-30a25cbf73cb" "a20069bc-29e2-5dfe-879f-ba66473f9669" "c61f46df-4504-4f23-8736-4f35298818a9" "cee3c0c4-f256-59b2-91af-36ab18240b0e" "4a205916-1df6-5aad-a7c6-5fc4a908191e" "202b9a1b-eed5-5692-bfd3-62c088a209f7" "6a7a85f3-6aba-5255-a219-0033c59fdaf7" "bcedcf39-e20b-4bf1-8165-b45139a8ad22" "1c75dad6-a0eb-5d48-a8ad-d70951f0d0a7" "3e17f3eb-ca05-56b0-b6f8-017a8a8f248e" "bb5489ab-0243-554b